Engineering drawings for measurement — NPL Guide 79 (@mech-npl-drawings: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_48E0H38P8GEB0XPX68MYXGGA48
David Flack and Keith Bevan, *Fundamental Good Practice in the Design and Interpretation of Engineering Drawings for Measurement Processes*, Measurement Good Practice Guide 79, July 2005, 99 PDF pages. [NPL publication](https://eprintspublications.npl.co.uk/3338/) and [official PDF](https://eprintspublications.npl.co.uk/3338/1/mgpg79.pdf).

Read the complete guide progressively for the connection between design, manufacture, drawing interpretation and inspection. Its datum, geometric-characteristic and measurement examples support a physical understanding of specifications. Historical standard references do not establish the applicable current edition for a new deliverable.

Retrieved outside the repository on 30 October 2026; publication information, contents and selected drawing/measurement passages were inspected. Crown copyright 2005, reproduced with permission as stated in the guide. Free institutional access is not a general Creative Commons adaptation licence. Keep the PDF external.

